WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.868
This provided script loads sample records into the
clinic schema Some

00:00:05.881 --> 00:00:08.763
of the SQL uses lookup and join patterns that are
taught in

00:00:08.789 --> 00:00:11.815
more detail later so you do not need to write this
loading

00:00:11.829 --> 00:00:16.854
script from memory Run it in the browser and inspect
the final

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:22.852
result Focus on what is happening conceptually
patients providers

00:00:23.036 --> 00:00:28.341
and services are inserted first The appointment
refers to existing patient and

00:00:28.355 --> 00:00:33.868
provider rows Appointment-service rows then connect
the appointment to services

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:41.729
The insert order follows the relationships we
designed If you use pgAdmin

00:00:41.966 --> 00:00:46.245
run the schema first and then the loading script
Parent data must

00:00:46.271 --> 00:00:49.495
exist before child rows that reference it can be
inserted
